# You Might Not Need an Effect

Reference: [You Might Not Need an Effect](https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).

Effects synchronize with **external systems** (DOM APIs, third-party widgets, non-React subscriptions). Do **not** use Effects to transform data for render or to react to user events.

## Prefer these instead

| Temptation | Do this |
|---|---|
| Sync state A from props/state B | Calculate during render: `const x = f(props, state)` |
| Expensive derived value | Calculate during render; rely on React Compiler (avoid manual `useMemo` by default) |
| Reset all state when an ID/prop changes | Remount with `key={id}` on a child component |
| Adjust one piece of state when props change | Store previous prop and adjust during render, or derive if possible |
| POST / notify / navigate on click | Put logic in the event handler |
| Notify parent of state change | Call parent callback from the event that caused the change |
| Chains of `setState` in Effects | Derive values or fold into the event handler |

## Good Effect uses

- Focus, scroll, measure DOM (`useLayoutEffect` when paint-sensitive)
- Subscribing to `window` / WebSocket / external store (prefer `useSyncExternalStore` when applicable)
- Imperative third-party widgets
- Data fetching only when not already handled by TanStack Query / route loaders

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — redundant state + Effect
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState('')
useEffect(() => {
  setFullName(`${firstName} ${lastName}`)
}, [firstName, lastName])

// ✅ GOOD — calculate during render
const fullName = `${firstName} ${lastName}`
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — sync mode from props in an Effect
useEffect(() => {
  if (forceEdit) setMode('edit')
}, [forceEdit])

// ✅ GOOD — derive when the prop must win
const mode = forceEdit ? 'edit' : (userMode ?? defaultMode)
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fetch/notify in Effect after click sets a flag
useEffect(() => {
  if (submitted) sendRequest(data)
}, [submitted, data])

// ✅ GOOD — do it in the click handler
async function handleSubmit() {
  await sendRequest(data)
}
```

## Project notes

- Follow `.cursor/rules/modular-react.mdc`: data loading belongs in hooks + TanStack Query, not `useEffect` in components.
- Do not add `useMemo`/`useCallback` by default; this app uses React Compiler.
